Third-Party Material
====================

The BSD 3-Clause grant in LICENSE covers this repository's own code. It does NOT
extend to the material listed below, which originates elsewhere and carries its
own terms. Anyone redistributing this repository must resolve these separately.

1. (RESOLVED) experiments/xtc_bridge/test_gpu_calib_cm.py previously carried five functions
   transcribed verbatim from psana `Detector/UtilsCommonMode.py`. psana declares no licence, so
   no grant attached to that code. The copy has been removed; the test now imports those
   functions from psana at run time and skips when psana is absent. No psana code remains in
   this repository.

2. glint/replica_gpu.py, glint/replica_gpu_batch.py
   Original lines, but written by reading PSI's fast-feedback-indexer (ffbidx)
   C++/CUDA source rather than clean-room from the publication. These SHIP.
   Recorded here because the derivation is not clean-room, not because the code
   is copied.

3. Derived data in-tree
   q-vectors derived from CXIDB entries 17 (experiments/frames_cxidb_clean.txt
   and duplicates) and 45. Redistribution terms for the underlying depositions
   are unresolved; entry 45 additionally depends on a geometry file associated
   with cxidb-62, which may carry a third set of terms.

Everything else with an apparent open-source lineage is original code
reimplementing a published algorithm -- for example peakfinder8.py (Barty 2014,
Cheetah) and peakfinder9.py (Gevorkov) -- which is cited, not third-party
material.
